curret idea:
write batched mcts
then run it in paralell to get multithreaded perforance and better gpu utilization

options:
individual tree traversal, node holds one game
- simpler mcts code
- requires game rewrite for single game performance - well desn't strictly require it.

paralell tree exploration, nodes store stats indexed by zorbist hash or move path
- more complicated mcts
- potentially faster
- no game engine rewrite


