implement update cap on low probability with gamma





each node holds a game and node stats.

nodes are looked up by hashing instead of path.

so we start of with n nodes. each steps untill they reach a leaf, accumulate into one model call.

select node from possible moves, 
compute its hash, lookup if it exists  --  so the function/class takes the current hash, current board state, and move to perform. the key trick is we do not use the game implementation to step, instead build all the logic for it inside the hash. it only needs to be able to do one move, and doenst need scores or anything else. that means that with the current game all it really needs is collision logic, as everything else is just placing marks. this way it can be near instant (hopefully). i reckon conditional logic for the hashes will be slower than just doing 2 xors always. write this implementation in a separate file i think.

if it doesnt clone current game
then step to it

this is my outline idea for mcts. by using hashing we will automatically combine same graph nodes, and achieve higher mcts efficiency. for now i want you to implement just hte zobrist hashing in a different rust file.